course: dictionary
lesson: 14452
title: Paramilitary
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from smaller parts, and the parts give you clues. Para- can mean beside or alongside. Military means to do with soldiers and the army. So paramilitary means something that works alongside the army, like an army, but is not the army itself.
explain: «The paramilitary group marched through the town, although it was not part of the country's army.» The word «although» tells you the group looked like soldiers but was not the official army. That contrast is the key clue.
explain: When you see paramilitary, ask two questions. Is the group organised like an army? Is it outside the normal army? If both answers are yes, the word fits. Then check by swapping in your meaning to see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Paramilitary means organised like an army, but not part of a country's official army.
fact: As a noun, «a paramilitary» means a member of such a group, or the group itself.
fact: Para- means beside or alongside, and military means to do with soldiers.
fact: Paramilitary groups have fought in places such as Northern Ireland during the Troubles, and in many wars.
fact: Some police forces have paramilitary units, which are trained in a more army-like way for dangerous jobs.
exercise: «The paramilitary group was organised like an army, but it was not part of the official army.» What does paramilitary mean? | Part of the country's official army | Peaceful and quiet | *Organised like an army but not part of the official army | A kind of musical instrument
exercise: «A paramilitary marched past the gate.» In this sentence, what kind of word is paramilitary? | Adverb, meaning quickly | Verb, meaning to march | *Noun, meaning a member of such a group | Adjective, describing a school
exercise: «The paramilitary group marched through the town, although it was not part of the country's army.» What clue tells you the group is not the official army? | *although it was not part of the country's army | the group | the town | marched through the town
test: Which definition fits paramilitary best? | A school club for reading | A government office for money | A type of weather | *Armed people organised like an army, but outside the normal army
test: Which sentence uses paramilitary as an adjective? | They paramilitaried the park all afternoon. | Paramilitary is the name of our village. | *The paramilitary training camp was hidden in the hills. | A paramilitary ran to the shop for milk.
exam: «The paramilitary group was armed and acted outside the normal army.» Why does this sentence warn the reader? | The group is cheerful and helpful to everyone | The group has no members at all | The group is a choir of children | *Armed people are acting outside the normal army
